{
  "payloads": [
    {
      "text": "### Overview of the Book\n**Title:** Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty  \n**Authors:** Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara  \n**Year:** 2021  \n**Publisher:** MIT Policy Press  \n**ISBN:** 978-0-26203-847-1  \n\n**Summary:**  \nThis 312-page technical monograph applies Bayesian inference and stochastic optimization to the design of public policies under conditions of deep uncertainty. The authors argue that traditional policy analysis frameworks, which rely on deterministic projections and point estimates, are inadequate when faced with non-stationary risks and contested model assumptions. The book introduces the 'adaptive policy envelope' framework, which treats policy commitments as probability distributions over possible outcomes instead of fixed directives. This allows for policy revisions based on new evidence without undermining credibility. The work includes three extended case studies focusing on climate adaptation policy in the Netherlands, pandemic response protocol design, and infrastructure investment under seismic risk.\n\n**Key Themes:**\n- Bayesian policy analysis\n- Deep uncertainty\n- Adaptive governance\n- Stochastic optimization\n- Policy design\n- Decision theory\n- Uncertainty quantification\n\n---\n\n### Authors\n#### Vasilis Papadimitriou\n- **Position:** Professor of Public Policy at Harvard Kennedy School\n- **Research Focus:** Bayesian policy analysis, adaptive governance, and deep uncertainty\n- **PhD:** MIT Operations Research, 2003\n- **Publications:** He has authored \"Stochastic Governance\" and other scholarly articles such as \"Adaptive Policy Envelopes under Deep Uncertainty\" and \"Bayesian Updating in Multi-Stakeholder Policy Contexts.\" He is also a co-editor of \"Uncertainty and Governance: A Reader\" published by MIT Press.\n\nFor more details, you can view his profile [here](https://openbooks.net/authors/vasilis-papadimitriou).\n\n#### Sakura Nishihara\n- Information specific to Sakura Nishihara wasn't retrieved in this search but may be available through academic databases or institutional pages if needed. \n\nThis monograph should serve as a valuable resource for your course on policy analysis under uncertainty, providing modern approaches to policy design.",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
  ],
